    {
      "name": "Giant Tarantula Venom",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [
        "poison"
      ],
      "description": "<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 23 Fortitude Saving Throw</p><hr /><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 8 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d10 Poison Damage damage (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 1d12 Poison Damage damage, Clumsy 1, and Off-Guard (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 2d6 Poison Damage damage, Clumsy 2, and off-guard (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> 2d6 poison damage and Paralyzed (1 round)</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Hair Barrage",
      "actions": 2,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>The tarantula flicks its legs, flinging spiky hairs in a 15ft Cone. This deals 4d6 Piercing Damage damage with a Basic DC 25 Reflex Saving Throw save.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Hazard Immunity",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>The shadowpact tarantula never triggers the reactions of hazards in its own lair and is immune to the negative consequences of damaging area effects created by hazards in its lair (so if a PC set off a hazard that released a Fireball inside its lair, it would not take damage from the <em>fireball</em> even if it was within the <em>fireball's</em> area).</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Knockdown",
      "actions": 1,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p><details><summary>See rules...</summary>\n<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p></details></p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
